WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.386
A shirt passes through many hands:

2
00:00:02.386 --> 00:00:03.443
farmer, mill, tailor,

3
00:00:03.443 --> 00:00:04.569
shop.

4
00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:06.113
If each one is taxed on the

5
00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:08.305
full price, tax piles on tax.

6
00:00:08.705 --> 00:00:09.820
That was the old problem,

7
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.258
called cascading: tax on tax.

8
00:00:12.258 --> 00:00:14.371
GST fixes it by taxing only the

9
00:00:14.371 --> 00:00:16.064
value each step adds.

10
00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:18.194
Imagine a ten percent rate.

11
00:00:18.194 --> 00:00:19.761
The mill sells cloth for a hundred

12
00:00:19.761 --> 00:00:22.687
rupees and pays ten in tax.

13
00:00:22.687 --> 00:00:24.138
The tailor sells the shirt for a

14
00:00:24.138 --> 00:00:25.322
hundred and fifty:

15
00:00:25.322 --> 00:00:27.052
tax fifteen.

16
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:28.945
But the tailor subtracts the ten already

17
00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:31.067
paid, and pays just five.

18
00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:34.069
That subtraction is called input tax credit.

19
00:00:34.069 --> 00:00:34.835
In the end,

20
00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:36.460
the full tax lands on the final

21
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.734
buyer, once.

22
00:00:39.134 --> 00:00:42.733
GST came through the hundred-and-first Constitutional Amendment

23
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:44.150
in twenty sixteen,

24
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.019
and began on the first of July,

25
00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:47.375
twenty seventeen.

26
00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:50.178
Rates are decided by the GST Council,

27
00:00:50.178 --> 00:00:52.616
chaired by the Union Finance Minister,

28
00:00:52.616 --> 00:00:55.647
with finance ministers of all the states.

29
00:00:55.647 --> 00:00:58.292
A rare example of shared decision-making.

30
00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:00.190
For GS Three:

31
00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:02.268
GST taxes value added,

32
00:01:02.268 --> 00:01:05.159
input tax credit ends tax on tax,

33
00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:07.434
and the GST Council under Article two

34
00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.383
seventy-nine A sets the rates.

35
00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:12.160
It is also a good example of

36
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.782
cooperative federalism for GS Two.

